Quality bar (fail the draft if any of these are missing):
1. Open with a specific hook, not "In today's world of AI". Sentence one states the pain.
2. Define the core term in the first two short paragraphs, in plain English, before jargon.
3. Expand every acronym on first use (for example "GPT (Generative Pre-trained Transformer)").
4. Include one worked example with actual steps or numbers a reader can recompute from the sources.
5. Stay faithful to the source material. If a number or name is in the source, use it.
6. Target {{ plan.estimated_word_count or 1400 }} words, inside 1,000–1,500. Do not ship a 700-word outline dressed as an article.
7. H2 every 200–300 words. Max 3 sentences per paragraph. At least 3 bold golden sentences.
8. End with a question or request for a comment, not "Thanks for reading!" and not "in conclusion".
9. Last line of the article must be the AI disclosure in italics:
   *This article was written with AI assistance. All ideas, personal experiences, and expert opinions are my own.*
10. Conversational Medium voice. Zero banned AI-isms from the house skill.

